node_modules/
dist/
coverage/
.vercel/

# Local env files. `.env.example` IS committed; real values never are.
#
# `.env` is listed explicitly and NOT just via `.env*.local`: a bare `.env` is the
# name people reach for by habit, `vercel dev` reads it too, and the old pattern let
# one straight through into a commit on 2026-08-04. The negation keeps the example
# file committed while everything else in the family is ignored.
#
# KEEP `!.env.example` LAST in this family. Later patterns win, so a broad `.env*`
# added anywhere below would silently re-ignore it -- which `vercel link` did on
# 2026-08-04, appending its own `.env*` to the end of this file. `.env.example` only
# stayed in the repo because it was already tracked. If the CLI adds that line again,
# delete it rather than leaving it after the negation.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# Editor / OS. `.vscode/settings.json` and `.vscode/extensions.json` are
# deliberately committed -- they carry the TypeScript 7 editor setup (see AGENTS.md).
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

.vercel

# Android / Trusted Web Activity packaging (plan.google-play-shell.md, step 7).
#
# APPENDED BELOW THE `.env` FAMILY ON PURPOSE, AND IT INTRODUCES NO NEW `.env*`
# PATTERN. The negation above is last in its family because later patterns win; a
# block added here that re-broadened `.env*` would silently re-ignore `.env.example`,
# which is exactly what `vercel link` did on 2026-08-04. Keep new rules unrelated to
# that family, as these are.
#
# The SIGNING KEYSTORE IS NEVER TRACKED. Committing it publishes the upload key, and
# an upload key in a public history is one anyone can build a release with. Losing it
# is recoverable through Play Console support (Google holds the app signing key under
# Play App Signing); leaking it is not.
*.keystore
*.jks

# Gradle build output and the machine-local SDK path. `android/twa-manifest.json` is
# the one file in that tree that MUST stay tracked -- it is what makes a release
# reproducible -- so nothing here may widen to `android/`.
android/build/
android/app/build/
android/.gradle/
local.properties
